UID:mudgirl-denver-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260829T083000Z
DTEND:20260829T123000Z
SUMMARY:Mudgirl Denver
DESCRIPTION:Mudgirl is an obstacle race dedicated to women. The Denver event takes place August 29th & 30th\, 2026 at Colorado National Speedway. Participation includes headband\, wristband\, bag\, finisher medal\, and tattoo. Minimum age is 7 years old (ages 7-13 require adult supervision). Saturday is sold out; Sunday still has availability.
LOCATION:Colorado National Speedway\, 4281 County Road 10\, Dacono\, CO 80514\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rock-hawk-trail-races-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260829T060000Z
DTEND:20260829T100000Z
SUMMARY:Rock Hawk Trail Races
DESCRIPTION:Rock Hawk Trail Races are held on the gorgeous\, thrilling and rolling trails of Castle Rock's Miller Park & Ridgeline Trail systems. While not overly technical\, these trails will challenge and excite runners while soaking up amazing views. This is an excellent race for both first-time and veteran trail runners\, and provides a nice test for those training for longer summer events. A portion of proceeds benefit open spaces and trails of Castle Rock and partner charities.
LOCATION:Philip S. Miller Park\, 1375 W Plum Creek Pkwy\, Castle Rock\, CO 80109
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:grand-traverse-mountain-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260905T060000Z
DTEND:20260905T100000Z
SUMMARY:Grand Traverse Mountain Run
DESCRIPTION:Point-to-point ultramarathon from Crested Butte to Aspen across the Elk Mountains with over 6\,000 feet of elevation gain. Follows the route of the Grand Traverse Backcountry Ski race. Fundraising event for Crested Butte Nordic\, a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization. General registration opens December 1\, 2026.
LOCATION:Start: Town Park\, Crested Butte\, CO | Finish: Ajax Park – 1001 S. Ute Ave\, Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golden-harvest-half-marathon-5k10k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260905T080000Z
DTEND:20260905T120000Z
SUMMARY:Golden Harvest Half Marathon & 5K/10K
DESCRIPTION:Family-friendly race organized by Bodies Race Company featuring multiple distance options including a Kids Dash. Includes custom race shirt\, finisher medal\, chip-timing with live results\, free photos\, and snacks at the finish line. Age group awards available for 5K/10K/Half Marathon participants. Virtual participation option available.
LOCATION:Parking Lot South of The Westin Westminster\, 10600 Westminster Blvd\, Westminster\, CO 80020
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-grand-traverse-bike-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260906T080000Z
DTEND:20260906T120000Z
SUMMARY:The Grand Traverse (Bike)
DESCRIPTION:The Grand Traverse Bike is a 40-mile point-to-point mountain bike race from Crested Butte to Aspen\, CO. Part of the Grand Traverse Triple Crown series (Ski\, Run\, Bike)\, the race is operated as a fundraising event for Crested Butte Nordic\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit. The route is partially based on historic mail routes connecting the Colorado mining towns of Crested Butte and Aspen from the 1880s. General registration opens at midnight on December 1st.
LOCATION:Crested Butte\, CO to Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ned-ned-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T080000Z
DTEND:20260912T120000Z
SUMMARY:Ned Ned Run
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating over 40 years\, this race explores the high-altitude trails around Nederland at over 8\,000 feet. Includes a family-friendly 5K road run.
LOCATION:151 East St\, Nederland\, CO 80466
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:black-squirrel-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T080000Z
DTEND:20260912T120000Z
SUMMARY:Black Squirrel Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Black Squirrel Trail Half Marathon takes place on the trails of Lory State Park northwest of Fort Collins\, Colorado. The 13.5-mile course with approximately 2\,000 feet of vertical gain offers a perimeter tour of the park with breathtaking views of Horsetooth Reservoir\, Fort Collins\, the Great Plains\, and Rocky Mountain peaks. The course features 12 miles of dirt singletrack and 1 mile of dirt road\, with terrain ranging from technical to non-technical hard-pack trails. Includes a post-race pancake breakfast\, finisher awards\, and a free 1-mile kids race.
LOCATION:Soldier Canyon Picnic Area\, Lory State Park\, Bellvue\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meadowgold-11k-5k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T090000Z
DTEND:20260912T130000Z
SUMMARY:MeadowGold 11K & 5K
DESCRIPTION:Trail running series race with well-marked routes\, aid stations\, and Northside Kitchen donuts at the finish.
LOCATION:Minturn\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:devil-on-the-divide-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T080000Z
DTEND:20260912T120000Z
SUMMARY:Devil on the Divide
DESCRIPTION:One of the most beautiful and challenging trail races in Colorado with breathtaking views of Clear Creek County and the Continental Divide. Participants reach over 13\,000 feet altitude with 6\,500+ feet of climbing for the 50K course and 3\,400 feet of elevation gain for the 22K. 100% point-to-point dirt courses\, majority single track trail. Prior ultra running experience required for 50K; trail running experience at high altitude recommended for 22K.
LOCATION:Guanella Pass\, Empire\, CO 80438
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lead-king-loop-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260913T080000Z
DTEND:20260913T120000Z
SUMMARY:Lead King Loop
DESCRIPTION:A spectacular fall running event through peak colors in the heart of the Elk Mountains. The 25K course winds through Lead King Basin\, past the iconic Crystal Mill\, and through the historic Town of Crystal. Also features the 8-Mile Quarry Climb along the Yule Marble Quarry Road. Includes post-race BBQ lunch\, beer (21+)\, custom shirt\, finisher medal\, and kids race. All proceeds benefit Marble Charter School.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-rabbit-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260918T090000Z
DTEND:20260918T130000Z
SUMMARY:Run Rabbit Run
DESCRIPTION:The Run Rabbit Run features two ultramarathon races: the 14th Annual 100 Mile Race on September 18\, 2026 (limited to 450 entrants with Tortoise and Hare divisions) and the 19th Annual 50 Mile Race on September 19\, 2026 (limited to 200 entrants). The 100 mile race offers the highest purse of any 100 mile race with $100\,000 overall ($20\,000 to winners). Registration is currently full; waitlist available. A charity race benefiting northern Colorado nonprofits.
LOCATION:Steamboat Ski Resort\, 2305 Mt Werner Cir\, Steamboat Springs\, CO 80487
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-the-rockies-road-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Run the Rockies Road Race
DESCRIPTION:The 50th Annual Run the Rockies Road 10k and Half Marathon features a downhill course along the Summit County Recreation Path through Ten Mile Canyon\, showcasing fall foliage. The 10K (6.2 miles) is 100% downhill with an 8:30 AM start\, while the Half Marathon (13.16 miles) is 75% downhill with an 8:00 AM start. Both races have a hard stop cutoff time of 11:30 AM. Registration includes commemorative gifts\, finisher items\, aid stations\, professional timing\, post-race food\, and post-race beer (21+).
LOCATION:Starts at Copper Mountain Far East Parking Lot\, ends at Frisco Historic Park\, 1 Main Street\, Frisco\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ascent-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ascent & Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The oldest continually held marathon in the United States (founded 1956). Runners start in Manitou Springs and travel 26.2 grueling mountain miles to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down. The sister race\, Pikes Peak Ascent\, is a 13.3-mile climb up the historic Barr Trail with approximately 7\,800 vertical feet of elevation gain.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fall-equinox-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T080000Z
DTEND:20260920T120000Z
SUMMARY:Fall Equinox Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Fall Equinox running event featuring Half Marathon and 5 Mile distances
LOCATION:Fort Collins\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T070000Z
DTEND:20260920T110000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Known as 'America's Ultimate Challenge\,' this race ascends to the 14\,115-foot summit of Pikes Peak before descending back to Manitou Springs. It is one of the most physically demanding marathons in the world due to the 7\,800-foot vertical climb.
LOCATION:Manitou Ave (City Hall)\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:west-line-winder-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DTEND:20260926T120000Z
SUMMARY:West Line Winder
DESCRIPTION:The West Line Winder 30K & 50K features miles of buttery single track and forest roads with glorious views of the Collegiate Peaks\, set on arid desert-style trails just outside of Buena Vista\, CO. Suitable for first-time trail runners to veteran ultramarathoners. Hosted by 14er Fest\, the event includes trail events\, clinics\, festival camping\, live music\, local libations\, and vendors.
LOCATION:Buena Vista\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golden-leaf-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DTEND:20260926T120000Z
SUMMARY:Golden Leaf Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Golden Leaf Half Marathon presented by ACG is one of the most beautiful foot races in the Rockies. This 13.3 mile half marathon traverses from Snowmass Village to the heart of Aspen on mountain trails and roads at the height of Colorado's breathtaking fall colors. Chosen by Trail Runner Magazine as one of America's 14 most scenic races and by Colorado Runner as a Best Half Marathon. Registration is SOLD OUT for 2026. Mass start at 8:00 AM with no waves. Requires valid CORSAR card for participation.
LOCATION:Snowmass Village to Aspen\, CO (mountain trails and roads)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cougar-ridge-classic-26k-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T070000Z
DTEND:20260926T110000Z
SUMMARY:Cougar Ridge Classic 26K Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:Point-to-point trail running race starting in Vail and finishing in Minturn. The 26K course features 3\,439' elevation gain with 78% singletrack terrain and stunning views of Mount of the Holy Cross and golden aspen groves. A new 14K option (Cougar Cub) also available starting at Eagle's Nest. Registration limited to 250 racers. Includes post-race party and lunch vouchers at participating Minturn restaurants.
LOCATION:Starting at Gravity Haus Vail\, 352 E Meadow Dr.\, Vail\, CO | Finishing at Town of Minturn\, 101113 Williams St.\, Minturn\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:crested-butte-ultra-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T060000Z
DTEND:20260926T100000Z
SUMMARY:Crested Butte Ultra
DESCRIPTION:Crested Butte Ultra traverses through the Gunnison National Forest featuring single track trails through beautiful mountain meadows\, stunning mountain ridges\, wildflowers\, and fall foliage. The race offers three distances with elevation gains ranging from 2\,280' to 8\,301'. All runners receive a custom race shirt\, custom BOCO hat\, and finisher's medal.
LOCATION:Crested Butte Community School\, 818 Red Lady Avenue\, Crested Butte\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:boulderthon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260823T000000Z
DTSTART:20260927T080000Z
DTEND:20260927T120000Z
SUMMARY:Boulderthon
DESCRIPTION:Colorado's Premier Fall Race. A boutique marathon experience with big-city energy & amenities set beneath Boulder's iconic Flatirons. Features lululemon finisher gear\, 100% hemp bibs\, recycled medals\, live music\, community cheer zones\, and an epic after-party on Pearl Street. Attracts 15\,000+ runners from all 50 states and 18 countries. Rated top 10 in America by USA Today and recognized by Runner's World.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
